I keep the earlier review's approve. I checked C13 against H03, H04, H05, H18, H19, H22 and H23 in ledger_digest.md and against progress-log #139 and #145-149. The core of C13 is not on any do-not-repeat list and is distinct on never-varied factors:
(a) both-seat k4 d4 on all 24 lists instead of the 8-list subset (H22 and H03 list this as untested);
(b) a walls-only search seat (H22's missing decomposition; grep finds no run with psearch under --a-agent and greedy under --b-agent);
(c) CRN k8 with 8-16 determinizations (H22 untested);
(d) nested within-turn search (not in the log; it differs from #147's horizon-2 lines);
(e) wall sets B (scr-gate479 499) and C (main seg_0460), never probed;
(f) pilot-v2 under the exact rule (H03's missing variant).

The earlier review has one concrete error. It accepted the set-A replays as the carrier for the exact trace. That replay has already been run. notes/scripts/walls_vs_humans.js now logs a per-turn prizeTrace, and runs/probe/sts_exact_chain.sh (10-21, 21:36-23:00, labelled 'Log #150' but not yet in progress-log.md) produced three files:
- runs/probe/sts_greedy_all24.jsonl: 576 games. All 576 match wvh_greedy_all24_g0-7.jsonl on winner and turns.
- sts_search_human_sub.jsonl: 192 games.
- sts_search_both_sub.jsonl: 166 of 192 games.
So J1 on set A at 8 games a pair, under the exact STS rule at every T, is already measured, and so are the subset searched cells. Replaying them again would be a pure repeat. The rest of the candidate stays distinct.

There were no earlier dedicated reviews to keep. C37 is in H11's family (N2/N10, expert iteration toward one-turn search; it also touches H05, H06, H14 and H65). Every configuration in H11's do-not-repeat list varies other factors than the ones C37 changes. The tested runs were exit-strong (--distill 1.0, 8 options x 4 lines), exit (0.3, 6 x 2), exit-h2 (horizon 2, margin 0.15) and --search-lethal. All of them used hard argmax CE toward one option (rl/train.py:247, 343-347). All gated on best-minus-worst > --search-margin (rl/metagame.py:582). All scored leaves with the live pilot's value: tsearch plays and values lines with RemoteAgent(0) (env/remote_worker.js, the greedy o0 agent). All normalised the loss over searched rows only (ce.sum()/S). All drew lines on independent re-deals, one rng.u32() seed per (option, line). All trained inside a drafted population.

C37 changes five of these, and none was ever varied:
(1) soft CMPO-style targets pi*exp(clip(A/tau)) and a KL, instead of a one-hot CE;
(2) a paired best-vs-chosen gate at 2 SE, instead of a best-minus-worst margin;
(3) a frozen fork-time leaf (or C12's V_eval), instead of the live pilot;
(4) a loss averaged over all rows at 0.05, which is about a 6x smaller dose than the 0.3 floor tested;
(5) CRN-shared worlds across options.
It also runs on a fixed human-free deck panel rather than a drafted population. The H11 and H14 verifiers name exactly this v4 as genuinely untested. The progress log has v4 only as a plan (#144 at line ~3809, #147 Next), and grep finds no CMPO, soft-target or frozen-leaf run. The H65 do-not-repeat ('raising the puzzle part through distilled one-turn search targets', which inflated Trainer-first puzzles at -37 Elo) is covered: C37 reads Elo and tempo alongside the puzzles. One small point: the H11 untested entry names 'Gumbel top-k' option sampling, and C37 drops it (it probes up to 8 options, random beyond that, as now). That is fine, but the write-up should not claim it tests the full v4 named in #144.
